       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. The risks at that level are GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the ceiling.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain.\n- **600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day). These suit moderate pain.\n- **1600 mg as a single dose**, if you meant a one-time dose. I'd still advise against it, because the usual single dose is 800 mg or less.\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away. For example, if 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. Take food into account too. Ibuprofen is usually given with food or milk to reduce GI irritation."
      }
